In the discussion, James inquired about "PLRs" mentioned in a paragraph regarding PPP ratios from the SSP dataset. I clarified that "PLRs" refers to "Price Level Ratios," which are used to convert GDP values from purchasing power parity (PPP) to market exchange rates (MER). This ensures that cost-of-living differences are accounted for in comparisons. I suggested that switching to recent PLRs published by the World Bank or IMF could provide a more accurate conversion, thereby addressing the concerns about outdated factors affecting the analysis. I also offered further clarification if needed.
